; Hit test of an entity against the player, then continue where the caller says
;
; Used by the enemy handlers (Death, Satan, the crusaders and the other entities), which JP here with their slot on
; the stack: SP points at the slot's two hit box words (+$C offset, +$E size; both words have y in the low byte and x
; in the high byte, in 2-pixel units, see #R$C100). The minimum corner of the entity's box is its position plus the
; offset, the maximum corner its position plus the size (the size is measured from the position, not from the offset
; corner). The two corners go to DE and BC and the code falls into the overlap test #R$A85F with IX = #R$A87A. HL is
; stored as the operand of the JP at #R$A880, so that #R$A87A goes on at the caller's address with SP just after the
; two words.
; .
; Hardware: none.
;
; DE Position of the entity: D = x, E = y (2-pixel units)
; HL Address to continue at after the test
; SP Slot address + $C (the hit box offset word)
@label=HitTest
@isub=LD (SmcHitContinue+1),HL
c$A851 LD ($A881),HL ; continuation address
 $A854 POP HL        ; hit box offset (y, x)
 $A855 ADD HL,DE     ; minimum corner = position + offset
 $A856 EX DE,HL      ; DE = minimum corner
 $A857 POP BC        ; hit box size (y, x)
 $A858 ADD HL,BC     ; maximum corner = position + size
 $A859 LD B,H        ; BC = maximum corner
 $A85A LD C,L        ;
 $A85B LD IX,$A87A   ; continue at #R$A87A after the test
; Entry point of #R$A600, #R$A822 and #R$B665 (which load IX themselves): the overlap test. Compares the box (D,
; E)..(B, C) with the player box #R$8516 (min x, max x, min y, max y of Jean) and jumps to IX with carry set when they
; overlap, clear when not.
@label=OverlapTest
*$A85F LD HL,($8516) ; H = player min x, L = player max x
 $A862 LD A,B        ; entity max x below the player min x: no
 $A863 CP H          ;
 $A864 JR C,$A877    ; no
 $A866 LD A,D        ; entity min x not below the player max x: no
 $A867 CP L          ;
 $A868 JR NC,$A877   ; no
 $A86A LD HL,($8518) ; H = player min y, L = player max y
 $A86D LD A,C        ; entity max y below the player min y: no
 $A86E CP H          ;
 $A86F JR C,$A877    ; no
 $A871 LD A,E        ; entity min y not below the player max y: no
 $A872 CP L          ;
 $A873 JR NC,$A877   ; no
 $A875 JP (IX)       ; overlap: carry is set by the last CP
*$A877 OR A          ; no overlap: carry clear
 $A878 JP (IX)       ;
